From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:03:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: macsmc: Offer the debugfs key list on every machine

The debugfs "keys" file lists every key the SMC reports with its type,
size and flags, and reads the 32-bit float T* and P* keys. Which keys a
machine has differs even between machines with the same SoC, so this
list is how the sensors for its device tree are found. It is created
only on M3 machines, together with the SoC die zone.

Create it on every machine. The file is root-only (0400), queries key
metadata, reads only readable float T* and P* keys and writes nothing;
the SoC die zone stays M3-only. On the J604 (T8132) hwmon lists one
temperature and the fan, and its other keys cannot be found without it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
index 7e0a2312d2..7852fe5270 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
@@ -1397,8 +1397,13 @@ static int macsmc_hwmon_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(hwmon->dev, PTR_ERR(hwmon->hwmon_dev),
 				     "Probing SMC hwmon device failed\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * The key list is how the sensors of a machine are found, on every
+	 * machine; the SoC die zone stays an M3 feature.
+	 */
+	macsmc_hwmon_debugfs_init(hwmon);
+
 	if (macsmc_hwmon_is_m3()) {
-		macsmc_hwmon_debugfs_init(hwmon);
 		ret = macsmc_hwmon_die_register(hwmon);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
